[{"id":126157,"sender_id":11,"sender_full_name":"Urs","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/b00d1ee17463af676c78974439b92471?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/2-Latest-Changes/topic/cyclic.20loop.20space/near/126157\">#10</a> I was going to finally add details on the <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi></mrow><mo>⊣</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathrm{Ext} \\dashv {\\mathrm{Cyc}}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathrm\">Ext</span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">⊣</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.8778em;vertical-align:-0.1944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathrm\">Cyc</span></span></span></span></span></span>-adjunction (stub now <a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/cyclic+loop+space#TheExtCycAdjunction\">here</a>) but I was stopped in my tracks since adding <code>tikzcd</code> code to the page doesn’t work anymore.</p>\n<p>Whatever I do, even rudimentary code like “<code>\\begin{tikzcd} X \\end{tikzcd}</code>”, it gives me an error message saying “The error was: unable to extract error”.</p>\n<p>Strangely, <code>tikzcd</code>-diagrams in existing entries still render, and can be copied into the Sandbox where they will still render, but making any edit whatsoever to them yields again the above error message.</p>\n<p>I have sent a message to the technical team on this. But if anyone here has an idea, let me know.</p>\n<p><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mtext> </mtext></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\,</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0em;\"></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span></span></span></span></p>\n<p>[edit: Looks like Christian Sattler fixed the bug with the <code>tikzcd</code> rendering.]</p>\n<p><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mtext> </mtext></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\,</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0em;\"></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span></span></span></span></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/revision/diff/cyclic+loop+space/18\">diff</a>, <a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/revision/cyclic+loop+space/18\">v18</a>, <a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/cyclic+loop+space\">current</a></p>","timestamp":1791019446,"subject":"cyclic loop space","stream_id":2,"display_recipient":"Latest Changes","reactions":[]},{"id":126158,"sender_id":11,"sender_full_name":"Urs","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/b00d1ee17463af676c78974439b92471?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/2-Latest-Changes/topic/cyclic.20loop.20space/near/126158\">#11</a> It may be time to move to another model and retain the nLab pages just as pointers to resources.  </p>\n<p>I’ll prepare now a pdf file with a LaTeX source .zip that constitutes a sizeable entry for “cyclification” and will link to it from the nLab page.</p>","timestamp":1791028121,"subject":"cyclic loop space","stream_id":2,"display_recipient":"Latest Changes","reactions":[]},{"id":126159,"sender_id":1002,"sender_full_name":"perezl.alonso","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/b47e415ea36ec5eb3afc8f0a568e2a5c?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/2-Latest-Changes/topic/cyclic.20loop.20space/near/126159\">#12</a> Would it be too complicated to have something like the arxiv which takes tex projects and processes them as html’s?</p>","timestamp":1791034343,"subject":"cyclic loop space","stream_id":2,"display_recipient":"Latest Changes","reactions":[]},{"id":126162,"sender_id":11,"sender_full_name":"Urs","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/b00d1ee17463af676c78974439b92471?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/2-Latest-Changes/topic/cyclic.20loop.20space/near/126162\">#13</a> Okay, experimentally, I added this pointer:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">n</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.4306em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">n</span></span></span></span>Lab materials: <em>Cyclification</em> (2026-10-06) [<a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/scl/fi/7lgs6n7dloourk6deluo5/Cyclification_26-10-06.pdf\">pdf</a>, <a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/scl/fi/93ia1v0h736nnzoc9ekt3/Cyclification_26-10-06.zip\">zip</a>]</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Just a start. To be refined.</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/revision/diff/cyclic+loop+space/19\">diff</a>, <a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/revision/cyclic+loop+space/19\">v19</a>, <a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/cyclic+loop+space\">current</a></p>","timestamp":1791049885,"subject":"cyclic loop space","stream_id":2,"display_recipient":"Latest Changes","reactions":[]},{"id":126163,"sender_id":11,"sender_full_name":"Urs","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/b00d1ee17463af676c78974439b92471?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/2-Latest-Changes/topic/cyclic.20loop.20space/near/126163\">#14</a> (P.S. As a teaser: The material in section 2.2.2 there has a curious consequence —</p>\n<p>It implies that for <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"script\">A</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathcal\">A</span></span></span></span> classifying charges in 11D, then the D7/<span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>B</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">S^1_B</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1.0894em;vertical-align:-0.2753em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0576em;\">S</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.8141em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.4247em;margin-left:-0.0576em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.0502em;\">B</span></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">1</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.2753em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span>-charge classified by <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"script\">A</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathrm{Cyc}^2(\\mathcal{A})</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1.1373em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathrm\">Cyc</span></span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.8873em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.1362em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">2</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathcal\">A</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span></span></span></span> (cf. Fig. 5 on <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2609.36048#page=43\">p. 43</a> of <em><a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/schreiber/show/K%20from%20M\">K from M</a></em>) is indeed the <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi></mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"double-struck\">Z</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathrm{SL}(2,\\mathbb{Z})</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathrm\">SL</span></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord\">2</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathbb\">Z</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span></span></span></span>-monodromy expected to characterize D7-branes in F-theory!)</p>","timestamp":1791050866,"subject":"cyclic loop space","stream_id":2,"display_recipient":"Latest Changes","reactions":[]},{"id":126166,"sender_id":78,"sender_full_name":"RodMcGuire","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/93dc0f9f03cdabb6b19a1522bd94c69f?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/2-Latest-Changes/topic/cyclic.20loop.20space/near/126166\">#15</a></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>12 something like the arxiv which takes tex projects and processes them as html’s?</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>latexml still can’t handle tikz fully. They are currently using AI tools to rewrite it in Rust.</p>\n<p>May 2026 arxiv <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2605.16562\">Scaling Accessible Mathematics on arXiv: HTML Conversion and MathML 4</a></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://bsky.app/profile/dginev.bsky.social/post/3mpw35h67zc2c\">Deyan Ginev Jul 5, 2026 thread on Bluesky</a></p>","timestamp":1791064513,"subject":"cyclic loop space","stream_id":2,"display_recipient":"Latest Changes","reactions":[]},{"id":126182,"sender_id":147,"sender_full_name":"Dmitri Pavlov","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/7c66d1b7cad17c58076e0f3d13220d63?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/2-Latest-Changes/topic/cyclic.20loop.20space/near/126182\">#16</a> Re <a href=\"#narrow/channel/2-Latest-Changes/topic/cyclic.20loop.20space/near/126157\">#10</a>, <a href=\"#narrow/channel/2-Latest-Changes/topic/cyclic.20loop.20space/near/126158\">#11</a>:</p>\n<p>nLab pages are more accessible than an ephemeral PDF posted on Dropbox (what happens when Dropbox shuts down? and Dropbox links can rot even before that).</p>\n<p>Currently available LLMs can debug code and automatically fix bugs like the one described in <a href=\"#narrow/channel/2-Latest-Changes/topic/cyclic.20loop.20space/near/126157\">#10</a>.</p>","timestamp":1791338525,"subject":"cyclic loop space","stream_id":2,"display_recipient":"Latest Changes","reactions":[]},{"id":126186,"sender_id":11,"sender_full_name":"Urs","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/b00d1ee17463af676c78974439b92471?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/2-Latest-Changes/topic/cyclic.20loop.20space/near/126186\">#17</a> The bug was kindly fixed by Christian Sattler. He writes it took him 2 hours. </p>\n<p>I should eventually upload those “materials” to the nLab server. Still experimenting with the format. Have added pointer to a second one at <em><a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/Morse%20theory\">Morse theory</a></em>:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">n</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.4306em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">n</span></span></span></span>Lab materials: <em>Morse–Bott Theory of Free Loop Spaces</em> (6 Oct 2026) [<a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/scl/fi/99wgtv05ixj00itvz2o12/Morse-Bott-free-loop-spaces_26-10-06.pdf\">pdf</a>, <a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/scl/fi/icxcl7eyaawv8axufjr51/Morse-Bott-free-loop-spaces_26-10-06.zip\">zip</a>]</li>\n</ul>","timestamp":1791351675,"subject":"cyclic loop space","stream_id":2,"display_recipient":"Latest Changes","reactions":[]},{"id":126187,"sender_id":147,"sender_full_name":"Dmitri Pavlov","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/7c66d1b7cad17c58076e0f3d13220d63?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/2-Latest-Changes/topic/cyclic.20loop.20space/near/126187\">#18</a> Re <a href=\"#narrow/channel/2-Latest-Changes/topic/cyclic.20loop.20space/near/126186\">#17</a>: Dropbox denies access with “Sign up for free\nTo keep Morse-Bott-free-loop-spaces_26-10-06.pdf secure, we need to confirm your identity”</p>","timestamp":1791353497,"subject":"cyclic loop space","stream_id":2,"display_recipient":"Latest Changes","reactions":[]},{"id":126189,"sender_id":11,"sender_full_name":"Urs","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/b00d1ee17463af676c78974439b92471?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/2-Latest-Changes/topic/cyclic.20loop.20space/near/126189\">#19</a> Fair. So I uploaded the files to the nLab server now; see the new entry: <em><a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/nLab%20materials\">nLab materials</a></em>.</p>","timestamp":1791356718,"subject":"cyclic loop space","stream_id":2,"display_recipient":"Latest Changes","reactions":[]}]